m using tools  made by humanity that range from simple  to complex to carve out portions of the  earth we have as a species for millennia  known how to perform the essential  action of canoe  struction through deconstruction known  as digging a hole  so which process was used to create the  Yaga clan pit looking at the pit itself  we can immediately gather a couple clues  about its construction just beneath the  surface of the pit we can see that it is  decorated with lights and lovely frilly  drapes of the same iconic red Yaga clan  color and above that it's even had a  smooth stone surface of some sort  constructed along the edges no rails to  prevent people from falling in but I'll  get to that in just a sec now it is  possible that these decorations and even  the smooth stone surfaces were simply  placed here along this  naturally-occurring pit but I have a  couple of reasons why I personally don't  think this pit was of natural occurrence  firstly the hole itself is a bit too  even if you look at naturally occurring  sinkholes out in the wild or even within  urban environments you will rarely if  ever find one that is both perfectly  circular in its opening and retains that  same circular dimension all the way down  the entirety of the cylindrical cavity  but in-game for as far down the pit as  were allowed to see aside from a couple  understandable shifts in the stone wall  the pit for the most part retains its  shape all the way down huh secondly  these decorations here seem to me to be  of some sort of significance don't they  the drapes have markings on them that I  haven't been able to locate elsewhere in  the hideout and the lights are uniquely  different models from all the other  lights found nearby this coupled with  the smooth stone surface along the edges  and specific lack of any device that  would catch someone especially their  leader if they were to fall in seems to  me to be very deliberate if basically  everything about the pit itself seems  de